 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 526675,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "A fish tank measures 75 cm long, 20 cm wide and 25 cm tall. The tank is 50 percent full. How many liters of water are needed to completely fill the tank?<br>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/a3c9661fa4d9c7cb.png\" alt=\"A rectangular prism represents a tank. The length, width, and height of the tank are marked 75 centimeters, 20 centimeters, and 25 centimeters. The tank is 50 percent full.\">\n</figure>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Step 1: Find the volume of the tank.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"V{\\text{ }} = {\\text{ }}L{\\text{ }} \\times {\\text{ }}W \\times H{\\text{ }} = {\\text{ }}\\left( {{\\text{75 cm}}} \\right)\\left( {{\\text{20 cm}}} \\right)\\left( {{\\text{25 cm}}} \\right){\\text{ }} = 37,500{\\text{ c}}{{\\text{m}}^3}\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 2: Convert the volume into liters.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"37,500\\cancel{{{\\text{cubic centimeters}}}}\\left( {\\frac{{{\\text{ 1 liter}}}}{{{\\text{ 1,000}}\\cancel{{{\\text{cubic centimeters}}}}}}} \\right) = 37.5{\\text{ liters}}\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 3: You only want half a tank of water, so divide the volume by two.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"37.5{\\text{ liters }} \\div {\\text{ }}2{\\text{ }} = {\\text{ }}18.75{\\text{ liters}}\"></span></p>\n<p>You need 18.75 liters of water.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "18.75 L"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
